  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mendubim Solar PV Power Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed operation consists of the design, construction, operation, and maintenance of the Mendubim Photovoltaic Power Plant (&#x201c;PV Power Plant&#x201d;) with a capacity of approximately 452.76 megawatts (&#x201c;MW&#x201d;) and a substation, as well as a 5.17-kilometer (&#x201c;km&#x201d;) long 230 kilovolts (&#x201c;kV&#x201d;) Transmission Line (&#x201c;TL&#x201d;) to connect the PV Power Plant to the Brazilian interconnected grid at the existing A&#xe7;u III Substation (&#x201c;The Project&#x201d;). The Project will be developed in the municipality of Ass&#xfa;, Rio Grande do Norte State, Brazil.</narrative>
  </description>
